{"type": "message", "id": "58b1a8fe", "parentId": "aa8a573b", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T11:20:28.356Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "SEC is blocking. Let me try to get the revenue figures from another source. I noticed from one of the earlier search results, the Q4 2023 update shows:\n\nFrom the electrek article: Q4 2023 revenue was $25.167 billion\nFrom the teslarati article: Q4 2023 revenue was $25.1B and EPS $0.71\n\nFrom the search results, I can also see the Tesla quarterly update data for Q1 2023:\nQ1 2023 Update PDF mentioned: \"Our operating income decreased YoY to $2.7B in Q1, resulting in a 11.4% operating margin.\"\n\n\nI'm cross-referencing the Q4 figures across multiple sources—CNBC, Teslarati, and Electrek all confirm revenue around $25.1B and net income of $7.9B. Now I need to find the quarterly revenue breakdown from the earnings reports to complete the picture.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_function_op10jv6933xk_1", "name": "web_fetch", "arguments": {"url": "https://digitalassets.tesla.com/tesla-contents/image/upload/IR/TSLA-Q4-2023-Update.pdf", "maxChars": 5000}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_function_op10jv6933xk_2", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "Tesla \"Q1-2023\" \"Q2-2023\" \"Q3-2023\" \"Q4-2023\" \"total revenues\" income statement quarterly revenue millions", "count": 5}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "minimax/minimax-m2.7", "usage": {"input": 1728, "output": 532, "cacheRead": 78843, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 81103, "cost": {"input": 0.0005184, "output": 0.0006384, "cacheRead": 0.00473058, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.005887379999999999}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775647217993, "responseId": "gen-1775647218-OyhK5o9VzSNzOAWBb43x"}}
